Rules for T.R.I.S.T.A.N. The full rules are in AGENTS.md (repository root) and docs/site-guide.md (the website, README and issues). Read them before you edit.

- Say what was run and what was not checked; use absolute dates and real numbers from the repository.
- Keep the author's employer, clients, secrets, account names and machine names out of everything public.
- Work on a branch and open a pull request. Never push to main. No tags or releases unless the owner asks.
- Never start a real claude, copilot, aws, az or ollama from a test or a check.
- The website is hand-written static HTML in docs/: no framework, no external scripts, accessible, usable at phone width, an em dash only in the title and none in new body text, and the name is written T.R.I.S.T.A.N.
- Run "bash scripts/check-site.sh" before you open the pull request.
